-- title:
--   Classes split by the unramified layer form ℤu
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $\Omega =$ `PadicAlgCl q` be the chosen algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, and let $K \subseteq \Omega$ be an intermediate field that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Let $r : (\Omega \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} \Omega) \to \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ be a group homomorphism subject to two compatibility hypotheses: `hlevel`, that for every intermediate field $E$ of $\Omega/K$ finite-dimensional over $K$ there is an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ with $r\sigma$ fixing $F$ pointwise fixes $E$ pointwise; and `hopen`, the converse direction, that for every such $F$ there is such an $E$ with every $\sigma$ fixing $E$ pointwise having $r\sigma$ fixing $F$ pointwise. Let $N > 0$ and put $L_N = K(\{\zeta \in \Omega : \zeta^{q^N-1} = 1\})$, assumed finite-dimensional and normal over $K$. Write $\mathrm{cH}^2 =$ `continuousH2 r (Rep.ofAlgebraAutOnUnits K Ω)`, the quotient of `levelCocycles₂` by the part of `levelCoboundaries₂` lying in it, with projection `continuousH2π`. The assertion is twofold. First, there is $u \in \mathrm{cH}^2$ whose additive order equals $\operatorname{finrank}_K L_N$ and such that the set of classes $\mathrm{cH}^2\pi(\mathrm{unitsInflate}_2\, L_N\, f)$, taken over all $f : \operatorname{Gal}(L_N/K)^2 \to \mathrm{Additive}\,(L_N)^\times$ lying in `cocycles₂ (Rep.ofAlgebraAutOnUnits K L_N)` whose inflation lies in `levelCocycles₂`, is exactly the set of integer multiples `AddSubgroup.zmultiples u`. Secondly, for every $N'$ divisible by $N$ with $L_{N'}$ finite-dimensional and normal over $K$, the corresponding set for $N$ is contained in that for $N'$.
--
--   This is the description of the part of the Brauer group of a $q$-adic field $K$ split by the unramified cyclotomic layer $K(\mu_{q^N-1})$: it is cyclic of order $[K(\mu_{q^N-1}):K]$, generated by the class of invariant $1/[K(\mu_{q^N-1}):K]$, and these subgroups increase along divisibility of $N$. Here the Brauer group is realised as the continuous $H^2$ attached to the level structure $r$, and the result feeds into [`groupCohomology.natCard_torsionBy_continuousH2_units_eq_of_padic`](thm.html#groupCohomology.natCard_torsionBy_continuousH2_units_eq_of_padic).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_groupCohomology_exists_split_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_eq_zmultiples_of_padic.lean

